      "content": "Shifting the narrative to view global governance as a direct threat to autonomy is a strong, though highly polarized, assertion. Proponents argue that modern threats—like climate change or pandemics—require transcending narrow state interests, while critics see this forced interdependence as the erosion of self-determination. Therefore, whether it is \"progress\" or \"threat\" depends entirely on whether one prioritizes absolute national control or shared global stability.",
      "source": "target",
